# Pairs with EventualKept in ReplicationReBootstrap. Reproduces production before the
# fix for #5689 (found under #5684): the applier's exact-identity dedupe memory was
# keyed by tree alone, so it outlived a shadow copy the drain had applied a row into.
# In a mutual re-seed, s applies r's row into copy 1; r cuts over to its own re-seed
# copy, so s's export fails and copy 1 is discarded; s re-drives into copy 2 and the
# same row is acknowledged as a duplicate without being applied, so s cuts over
# without it.
MODULE: EventualKeptDedupeOutlivesShadowCopy
TARGET: EventualKept
CLASS: Temporal
SUMMARY: the drain's dedupe memory is not scoped to the shadow copy, so a re-driven drain skips a row the aborted copy took with it
PERTURBS: ShadowRow
BOUNDS: Mutual = TRUE

--- FIND
           seen == [w |-> Id(u), c |-> cid[x]] \in dd[x]
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: an identity applied into any earlier copy of the tree counts as seen.
           seen == \E m \in dd[x] : m.w = Id(u)
--- END